2,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxODk4NjgzODMy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/labels/Cython","name":"Cython","color":"e99695","default":false,"description":"Issues with the internal Cython code base"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":15,"created_at":"2024-09-10T21:55:42Z","updated_at":"2024-12-07T01:25:47Z","closed_at":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"body":"### Describe your issue.

When multiplying a `Rotation` object by something other than a `Rotation`, we get a `TypeError`. This is bad because no other class can define `__rmul__` for rotations now.

### Reproducing Code Example

Say I have this simple class:

```python
class Isometry3(namedtuple("Isometry3", ["rotation", "translation"])):
    def apply(self, vec: ArrayLike) -> np.ndarray:
        return self.rotation.apply(vec)

    def __mul__(self, other: Union["Isometry3", Rotation]) -> "Isometry3":
        if isinstance(other, Rotation):
            other = Isometry3(other, np.zeros(3))
        return Isometry3(
            self.rotation * other.rotation,
            self.rotation.apply(other.translation) + self.translation,
        )

    def __rmul__(self, other: Union["Isometry3", Rotation]) -> "Isometry3":
        if isinstance(other, Rotation):
            other = Isometry3(other, np.zeros(3))
        return other * self

    def inv(self) -> "Isometry3":
        rinv = self.rotation.inv()
        return Isometry3(rinv, -rinv.apply(self.translation))
```

There is no reason why I shouldn't be able to do the following:

```
r = Rotation.from_euler("xyz", [1, 2, 3], degrees=True)
i = Isometry3(r, [1, 2, 3])
i * r # This works fine, treats `r` as an isometry with no translation
r * i # This does not work fine
```

```
TypeError: Argument 'other' has incorrect type (expected scipy.spatial.transform._rotation.Rotation, got Isometry3)
```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21541/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21541/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},"comment":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/comments/2524741941","html_url":"https://github.com/scipy/scipy/issues/21541#issuecomment-2524741941","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21541","id":2524741941,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABZIoc6WfIE1","user":{"login":"lucascolley","id":51488791,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNDg4Nzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51488791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley","html_url":"https://github.com/lucascolley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-07T01:25:46Z","updated_at":"2024-12-07T01:25:46Z","author_association":"MEMBER","body":"Thanks @Kai-Striega ! That makes sense. 

